<v Daniel>Which is a huge leap.</v>

13
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:24.625
<v Maya>It's massive. We used to test AI with standardized multiple choice questions like law exams or medical boards. Now we are basically throwing them the keys to the lab.</v>

14
00:01:25.165 --> 00:01:33.950
<v Daniel>Right. But to really get why this REE paper is such a big deal, we have to look at the timeline. Because the leap in capability over just the last two years is, well, it's wild.</v>

15
00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:37.452
<v Maya>Yeah, let's set that context. How fast are we actually moving here?</v>

16
00:01:38.239 --> 00:01:39.880
<v Daniel>So go back to 2024. There</v>

17
00:01:40.381 --> 00:01:43.743
<v Maya>was a benchmark called MLE Bench from OpenAI.</v>

18
00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:48.406
