133
00:13:23.858 --> 00:13:29.623
<v Daniel>It's the ultimate engineering versus science debate. If science is just finding the optimal path to a known metric, then</v>

134
00:13:29.863 --> 00:13:30.103
<v Maya>yes,</v>

135
00:13:30.704 --> 00:13:32.385
<v Daniel>the AI is doing science beautifully.</v>

136
00:13:32.605 --> 00:13:35.528
<v Maya>Right, but what if true science is questioning the metric itself?</v>

137
00:13:35.987 --> 00:13:49.459
<v Daniel>Exactly. Iterative improvement against an automated scorer captures optimization, but it doesn't capture the messy, subjective reality of noticing an ambiguous result and realizing it's a totally new discovery.</v>

138
00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:55.305
<v Maya>Which brings us to the limitations we absolutely have to acknowledge so the listener gets the full picture.</v>

139
00:13:55.670 --> 00:14:03.137
